Jason C. DeWilde wrote:

> Tradition? Are you referring to a cultural tradition, or is the lizard
> corpse some sort of throwback to an earlier [roguelike] game?

Googling through posts to net.games.hack and rec.games.hack from the mid-80s
returns no posts giving a reason why it should be lizards.  The best I can
do is give some history, as reflected in old source distributions.

Hack 1.0 - First appearance of the cockatrice.  Stoning by hissing is an
instakill in this version, with a chance of 1/5 per hiss.

Hack 1.0.2 - First appearance of the "dead lizard," as it was then called,
and of the effect of the new moon on stoning.  The lizard is a found object
rather than a corpse of a slain monster.  Eating the lizard has no effect
on stoning (but does diminish confusion); carrying it in one's pack merely
cancels the effect of the new moon.  The chance of stoning by hissing is
reduced to 1/20 per hiss, but it is still an instakill.

Hack 1.0.3 - Stoning by hissing now starts a timer rather than killing
instantly.  Eating the lizard still has no effect on stoning, nor is prayer
effective; the only way to cancel stoning in progress is to eat an acid
blob.

NetHack 1.3d - Eating a lizard cures stoning if the DGKMOD symbol is defined
at compile time.  This is the default.  Self-polymorph (first implemented
here) cures stoning, if you "feel like a new (wo)man".

NetHack 2.3e - Prayer can now cure stoning.

NetHack 3.0.0 - First appearance of the cockatrice egg.  Stunning is now a
distinct condition from confusion; lizards diminish stunning as well as
confusion.  Lizard corpses as a cure for stoning no longer depend on the
DGKMOD option.  Chance of stoning by hissing is now 1/10 per hiss. 
Self-polymorph to a stoning-resistant monster cancels stoning, as does
eating acidic corpses other than the acid blob.

NetHack 3.0.6 - First appearance of live lizards.  The lizard corpse is no
longer randomly generated.

NetHack 3.1.0 - Stoning a non-stone golem (including you, if polymorphed)
now turns it into a stone golem.

NetHack 3.1.1 - Monsters can now hit you with cockatrice corpses.  This does
not unconditionally start stoning, but is subject to the same conditions as
hissing.

NetHack 3.2.0 - A hit with a cockatrice corpse now unconditionally starts
stoning.  Monsters can now cure stoning by eating a lizard or acidic
corpse.  Self-polymorph into any golem while stoned instantly turns you to
a stone golem.

NetHack 3.3.0 - First appearance of the chickatrice, the potion of acid and
the stone to flesh spell.  Monsters can now throw cockatrice eggs at you.

NetHack 3.4.0 - Eating the brain of a petrifying monster (as a mind flayer)
now starts stoning.

